    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-1",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Rendered impact — which rendered files a Change Set changes",
      "prov:value": "> Skill id: `rendered-impact` · Package: `sdlc-core` · Bean: `bnjs` · Epic: `q4jm` · Issue #971",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#971"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-2",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The owner's rulings this follows",
      "prov:value": "- 2026-10-06: *\"for a Change Set ... and Issue -> create PR with change set.\n  see a list of rendered justthedocs files (fhir IG, whatever) that changed\n  due to the described changeset. use that as part of review process of\n  changeset PR approval.\"*\n- 2026-10-06: *\"each renderer should be able to give you from list of input\n  changed files, the list of output changed rendered files ... from the\n  dependency cone\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-3",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The owner's rulings this follows",
      "prov:value": "- 2026-10-06: the public-comment Change Set (`changeset/1.0.0`) is the Change\n  Set for ANY folio change, and the rendered list is one of its fields.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-4",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The owner's rulings this follows",
      "prov:value": "- 2026-10-06: *\"original stays in library/ ... materialized to folio/ to make\n  changes on\"*.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-5",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The contract: `rendered-impact/v1`",
      "prov:value": "**Index files are listed and marked, not dropped.** The reviewer's list\n   (`reviewList`) leaves out `role: index` (search data, sitemaps, an\n   artefact index) because the owner reviews content, not indexes."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The renderers today",
      "prov:value": "| renderer | maps | how | status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `fhir-ig-pages` | `.fsh`, `.cql`, `input/pagecontent/*.md` | `fsh-cone` forward cone → SUSHI's `fsh-index.json` → AST artefact page + served JSON; a page → itself and every page that includes it | in the FHIR layer, documented with its AST tooling (`skill_fetch ig-ast-delta`) |\n| `document-site`, `public-comment-site`, `library-site` | a block, a document/chapter/section manifest, `media/*`, the public-comment store, a file in a declared library entry or a folio `review-anchors.json` naming one (the entry's Document view and `doc.json`; its `structure.json` also the library index) | loaded from the published `changeset.json` (each changed block's label and file) and `outline.json` (the documents), never from source: a block lands on its document's page, anchored at its label (`anchors`) — on a LAZY page (`outline.json` `lazy`, bean v433) on its `blocks/NNN.json` chunk and `index.hydrated.html` instead, and a block added, removed, renamed or moved reshapes the shell and every chunk from its position on; a file no builder of the site reads is an input with no page: each builder in the folio's build command exports `siteReads` (the folio; the comment store; every directory of a typology holding a kind it renders), and a file outside all of them, the submodules, `.github/` and the root's non-Markdown files reaches nothing — so `beans/` reaches no page, while `todos/`, whose pages are rendered, still may."
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The renderers today",
      "prov:value": "**Measured on the docs-site renderer** (this repository's site, two local builds, 2026-10-06): a page, a data file read through an include, an include, a stylesheet and a script gave 8 predicted files and 8 measured. 7 were confirmed.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The renderers today",
      "prov:value": "**Measured on the FHIR renderer** (a real IG, bean `c65n`):\n- An FSH edit to one PlanDefinition gave 4 predicted files and 3 measured: 0 missed, and 1 unconfirmed (the artefact page, rule 3).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean c65n"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "In the review process",
      "prov:value": "The review page shows it under the list, as the PR comment does: a run\n  started by dispatch finds its PR from the branch, so the comment is not\n  lost when no `pull_request` event started the run (bean `ehh6`).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean ehh6"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "sdlc/skills/sdlc-core/rendered-impact.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "In the review process",
      "prov:value": "- **Show**: every docs-site preview also carries `branches/<slug>/changes/`\n  (`cat-harness-tools/scripts/staging-changes.ts`, owner 2026-10-14): the\n  changed sources, with a re-pinned mount in `index.lock.json` expanded into\n  the files its repository changed between the two pins (a re-pin handed to\n  a renderer as one JSON line predicts nothing); the cone's files and its\n  `undetermined` inputs; and the build diffed against the site at the\n  `gh-pages` root, its `missed` files listed as **changed, not in the cone**.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-14"
      ]
    }
